{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791534859,"nonce":"2mwcTVcNqz7gBE7si4Y+Q7WjukM=","title":"User observed about 1% idle CPU in Demo.hx and Interactions.hx. WindowedApp.loop currently waits at most 0.1 seconds even with no animation, dirty frame, or deadline, then runs scheduler.tick, theme.tick and tree.flush. This produces about ten wakeups per second without input.","message":"Sequential macOS diagnostic probes reused Demo.card and Interactions.page in inactive windows. Instrumented wait logging and Ash --jit-log, 8 second warmup then three 8 second samples, 35 second total lifetime:\n- Demo current: 345 wait calls, CPU 0.054/0.096/0.029%; diagnostic longer wait: 4 calls, 0.0010/0.0007/0.0022%.\n- Interactions current: 347 calls, CPU 0.042/0.472/0.013%; diagnostic longer wait: 3 calls, 0.0186/0.0003/0.0029%.\n- Interactions current footprint rose 159-\u003e188-\u003e169 MiB during the samples with JIT activity; longer-wait probe stayed around 154 MiB.\n\nThese are instrumented hybrid-runtime diagnostics, not a claim of exactly reproducing a sustained 1% CPU in the unmodified foreground app. Periodic logging contributes work. No input was sent, and long waits still obeyed timer/close deadlines. Earlier minimal-window runs disabling idle GC did not remove the periodic-loop activity; do not disable GC as a fix.\n\nProduction change must provide wakeups for background reactive changes, scheduler timers, invalidate/quit, GPU/media completions, and hot reload. Changing 0.1 to an indefinite wait alone can miss work. xwindow's macOS request_redraw only records Asked and is not a general blocked-wait wakeup. Existing Ash issue 4855ac5 also tracks pending Future completion with a macOS window. The old hlwindow per-poll event overhead issue d79d7bf is already fixed.\n\nLocal reproducer/source and logs: .ashui/memory-comparison/source/IdleScene.hx, idle-scenes.py, idle-093116. Keep separate from the shader-memory milestone 7c81996 (d701ddf) and hlwgpu HXSL expansion issue 0d9a25c.","files":null}]}